<div class="panel-body">
<p>Chris Ericksen was drafted by the Chicago Cubs in 2003. He has retired from baseball.</p>
<p>Jake Gloude- Western Illinois University.</p>
<p>Matt Miles- Calumet College of St. Joseph (IN).</p>
<p>Dirk Miller- Robert Morris College (IL).</p>
<p>Kevin Peller- Western Illinois University.</p>
<p>Mark Schuit- Millikin University in St. Louis, MO.</p>
<p>Ryan Sickles- Gardner-Webb University in Winston-Salem, NC. He is now assistant coach at South Suburban College.</p>
<p>Bill Wheeler was drafted by the Toronto Blue Jays in 2003. He is now retired from baseball.</p>
<p>Eric Woerheide- University of Sciences in Philadelphia, PA.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse2002" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">2002<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse2002" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Paul Ameilo- Robert Morris College (IL).</p>
<p>Justin Clarke- University of Wisconsin-Parkside.</p>
<p>Jim Healy- University of Wisconsin-Parkside.</p>
<p>Chris Hill- University of South Carolina, Spartanburg.</p>
<p>Jim Landini- Robert Morris College (IL).</p>
<p>Mike Lynch was drafted by the Los Angeles Dodgers in 2002. Now retired from baseball.</p>
<p>Eric Miller- Robert Morris College (IL).</p>
<p>Joe Nourie- Southeast Missouri State University.</p>
<p>Justin Papp- St. Xavier University (IL). He is now retired from baseball.</p>
<p>Pete Retsos- University of Northern Iowa.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse2001" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">2001<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse2001" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Adam Churchill- Olivet Nazarene University (IL).</p>
<p>Tom Cunningham- Robert Morris College (IL).</p>
<p>Dan Cunningham- University of Louisville (KY).</p>
<p>Jerrel Hughes- University of Arkansas-Pine Bluff.</p>
<p>Jon Moench- Dana College in Blair, NE.</p>
<p>Cliff Novak- University of Louisville (KY).</p>
<p>Ryan Rapp- Culver-Stockton College in Canton, MO.</p>
<p>Phil Wail- Barton College (NC).</p>
<p>Anthony Walker- Calumet College of St. Joseph (IN).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse2000" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">2000<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse2000" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Joshua Hearn- Iowa State University.</p>
<p>David Rodriguez- Culver-Stockton College in Canton, MO.</p>
<p>Thom Stapleton- University of Wisconsin-Parkside.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1998" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1998<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1998" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Dan Jackson was drafted by the Chicago Cubs in 1998. Now retired from baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1997" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1997<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1997" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Scott Frawley was drafted by the Atlanta Braves in 2006. Now retired from baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1996" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1996<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1996" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Rob Mackowiak was drafted by the Pittsburgh Pirates in 1996. Made his MLB debut on May 19, 2001 for the Pittsburgh Pirates. Played with the Chicago White Sox in 2006 and part of 2007. In July of 2007. he was traded to San Diego Padres. Played for the, Washington National and Cincinnati Reds in 2008. In 2010, he was hired as hitting coach for the Windy City ThunderBolts. Now retired from baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1994" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1994<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1994" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Julius Matos was drafted by the Cleveland Indians in 1994. Made his MLB debut on May 31, 2002 as a second baseman for the San Diego Padres. In 2011, Matos joined the AA Trenton Thunder as their hitting coach. Julius is now retired from professional baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1993" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1993<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1993" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>A relief pitcher, Tim Byrdak attended Rice University where he played college baseball. He was drafted by the Kansas City Royals in 1994. Tim made his MLB debut on August 7, 1998 for the Kansas City Royals. He went on to pitch for the Baltimore Orioles, Detroit Tigers, Houston Astros and New York Mets. Byrdak is now retired from professional baseball.</p>
<p>Vince Griffin was drafted by the Cleveland Indians in 1993. He is now retired from baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1992" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1992<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1992" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>John Lewandowski was drafted by the Cleveland Indians in 1992. He has retired from baseball.</p>
<p>Clint Gagnon was drafted by the Atlanta Braves in 1992. He is now retired from baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1991" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1991<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1991" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Rob Mahay was drafted by the Boston Red Sox in 1991. Rob made his MLB debut on May 21, 1995 for the Boston Red Sox. In 2001 and 2002, Mahay pitched for the Chicago Cubs. He is now retired from professional baseball after 16 years.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="panel panel-default">
<div class="panel-heading">
<h4 class="panel-title"><a class="accordion-toggle" href="#collapse1989" data-toggle="collapse" data-parent="#accordion">1989<i class="indicator fa fa-angle-double-down fa-lg pull-right"></i></a></h4>
</div>
<div id="collapse1989" class="panel-collapse collapse">
<div class="panel-body">
<p>Steve Munda was drafted by the New York Yankees in 1991. He is now retired from baseball.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>For more information on players that graduated before 1989, contact <a href="mailto:sruzich@ssc.edu"><i class="fa fa-envelope-o"></i> Coach Ruzich</a> at (708) 596-2000 ext. 5843.</p>
					</div>
									
									
					
					
				</article>
			</main>
		</div>
		
		
		

				
		
	</div>
</div>



			
			
